      "content": "**GridFlow CLI Quick Start Guide**\n\n### Installing GridFlow CLI\n\nTo get started with GridFlow CLI, install it using the following command:\n\n```bash\ncurl -sL https://gridscale.io/install.sh | sh\n```\n\n### Configuring GridFlow CLI\n\nAfter installation, you need to set up your GridFlow token in your shell configuration file. Add the following line to your `~/.bashrc` or `~/.zshrc`:\n\n```bash\nexport GRIDFLOW_TOKEN=your_token_here\n```\n\nReplace `your_token_here` with your actual GridFlow token.\n\n**Configuring GridFlow CLI**\n\nTo configure GridFlow CLI, run the following command:\n\n```bash\ngridflow config\n```\n\nThis will prompt you to enter your GridFlow token. Enter the token you added to your shell configuration file.\n\n**Basic Workflow**\n\nHere's a step-by-step guide to get you started:\n\n1. Initialize a new project using `gridflow init`. This will create a basic directory structure for your project.\n2. Navigate to your project directory using `cd path/to/your/project`.\n3. Configure your project settings using `gridflow config`. You can specify values for common settings such as the project name",
